// The `: NSObject` here is load-bearing, and the symptom of dropping it is nasty. The
// framework exports `_OBJC_CLASS_$__TtC12SourceEditor18SourceEditorGutter`, so this class is
// NSObject-rooted and must be released through the Objective-C dealloc chain. Declared as its
// own root it constructs fine, answers every call fine, and then crashes when it is
// *deallocated* — which is why a gutter kept alive for the process's lifetime hides the bug
// entirely. Adding `@objc deinit` does NOT fix it; only the superclass does.
// `SourceEditorLayoutManager` has no such symbol and is correctly a native Swift class.
@_hasMissingDesignatedInitializers @objc public class SourceEditorGutter : ObjectiveC.NSObject {
